-- Q666: Advanced Revenue and Intangibles [easy/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under ASC 606-10-55-36 through 55-40, an entity that arranges for goods to be provided without controlling them before transfer is an agent. Agents report revenue net (commission only) because they do not bear inventory risk, set prices, or take possession.
Wrong (A): A principal controls the goods before transfer and reports gross revenue, which does not apply when the entity never obtains control.
Wrong (C): A consignee holds goods on behalf of the consignor but still recognizes revenue upon sale; this role is distinct from the agent arrangement described.
Wrong (D): A lessor provides property under a lease agreement, which is governed by ASC 842, not the principal-agent framework of ASC 606.$EXPL$
