-- Q671: Advanced Revenue and Intangibles [medium/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under ASC 360-10-35-17, the recoverability test (Step 1) compares the asset''s carrying amount to the sum of undiscounted expected future cash flows from its use and eventual disposition. If undiscounted cash flows exceed carrying amount, no impairment exists and no further testing is needed.
Wrong (A): Fair value is used in Step 2 to measure the impairment loss, not in Step 1 to test recoverability.
Wrong (C): Discounted cash flows may be used to estimate fair value in Step 2, but Step 1 specifically requires undiscounted amounts.
Wrong (D): Net realizable value applies to inventory under ASC 330, not to long-lived asset impairment testing under ASC 360.$EXPL$
