-- Q672: Advanced Revenue and Intangibles [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under ASC 350-20-35, goodwill impairment losses are permanent and cannot be reversed under U.S. GAAP, even if the reporting unit''s fair value subsequently recovers. This conservative treatment reflects the difficulty of distinguishing recovery of original goodwill from internally generated goodwill.
Wrong (A): Writing goodwill back up upon improvement is prohibited; once impaired, the reduced amount becomes the new carrying value.
Wrong (B): Reversal in a subsequent fiscal year is not permitted regardless of how quickly conditions improve.
Wrong (D): The SEC does not have an approval mechanism for goodwill reversal; the prohibition is absolute under GAAP.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 672;

-- Q673: Advanced Revenue and Intangibles [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under ASC 606-10-55-54, a license of functional intellectual property provides the customer a right to use the IP as it exists at the point of transfer. Because the perpetual license functions independently without Vertex''s ongoing involvement, revenue is recognized at the point in time when control transfers to Kepler.
Wrong (A): Over-time recognition applies to symbolic IP (e.g., brand licenses) where the customer''s benefit depends on the licensor''s ongoing activities, not functional IP.
Wrong (C): Straight-line recognition over the license period is not required for a perpetual license of functional IP that transfers at a point in time.
Wrong (D): Installation by the customer is not a criterion for revenue recognition; control transfers when the license is delivered.$EXPL$
