-- Q674: Advanced Revenue and Intangibles [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under ASC 606-10-32-34, the residual approach determines SSP as the total transaction price minus the sum of observable SSPs of other obligations. It is permitted only when the SSP of a good or service is highly variable (sold at a wide range of prices) or uncertain (not yet established in the market).
Wrong (A): The adjusted market assessment approach estimates SSP based on observable market prices and is used when market data is available, not when SSP is highly variable or uncertain.
Wrong (B): The expected cost plus margin approach estimates SSP from the entity''s costs plus an appropriate margin, also requiring reasonably determinable inputs.
Wrong (D): Historical cost is not an SSP estimation method recognized under ASC 606.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 674;

