-- Q678: Stock Compensation and Business Combinations [medium/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under ASC 718-20-35-7, when stock options expire unexercised, the APIC -- stock options balance is reclassified to general APIC (or APIC -- expired options). No reversal of previously recognized compensation expense occurs because employees rendered the required service during the vesting period.
Wrong (A): Reversing to compensation expense would reduce prior-period expense, which is prohibited because the service was already provided regardless of exercise.
Wrong (C): Writing off to retained earnings is incorrect; the reclassification stays within equity components of APIC, not retained earnings.
Wrong (D): Expired options have no value to return; the equity balance is reclassified within the company''s accounts, not distributed to employees.$EXPL$
