-- Q691: Advanced Consolidations [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under ASC 810-10-45-18, 100% of unrealized intercompany profit from downstream sales must be eliminated in consolidation, regardless of the NCI percentage. The full elimination is charged to the parent because the parent initiated the sale, and consolidated statements must present the entity as if the intercompany transaction never occurred.
Wrong (A): Elimination applies specifically to the unrealized portion (unsold inventory with embedded profit), not conditioned on whether goods remain in subsidiary inventory generally.
Wrong (B): Proportionate elimination applies to upstream sales where the subsidiary initiates the transaction, not to downstream sales initiated by the parent.
Wrong (D): All intercompany sales require elimination in consolidation regardless of which entity controls the transaction.$EXPL$
