-- Q693: Advanced Consolidations [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under ASC 810-10-25-38, the primary beneficiary of a VIE must have both: (1) power to direct the activities that most significantly affect the VIE''s economic performance, and (2) the obligation to absorb potentially significant losses or right to receive potentially significant benefits. Both criteria must be met.
Wrong (A): Majority voting ownership applies to the voting interest model, not to VIE consolidation, which is determined by variable interests rather than equity votes.
Wrong (C): Being the largest equity holder does not automatically make an entity the primary beneficiary; the dual power-and-economics test must be satisfied.
