-- Q697: Advanced Consolidations [medium/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under ASC 810-10-45, when one affiliate holds bonds issued by another, the consolidated statements treat the debt as constructively retired on the intercompany acquisition date. The bond payable and bond investment are eliminated, along with intercompany interest, and any difference creates a constructive gain or loss.
Wrong (A): The bonds are not treated as issued to external parties because, from the consolidated entity''s perspective, the debt has been effectively retired.
Wrong (C): The bonds were not converted to equity; constructive retirement eliminates the debt entirely rather than reclassifying it.
Wrong (D): The bonds did exist as legal obligations; the constructive retirement is an accounting treatment for consolidation purposes, not a denial of their existence.$EXPL$
