-- Q698: Advanced Consolidations [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under ASC 810-10-45, because the 2024 elimination was made on the consolidation worksheet (not on the books), the 2025 consolidation must adjust beginning retained earnings to reverse the prior-year elimination entry. This ensures the profit recognized on the subsidiary''s books in the current year is properly reflected in consolidated beginning balances.
Wrong (A): Ending inventory does not contain unrealized profit because all goods were resold to external customers by year-end 2024; there is nothing left to eliminate.
Wrong (C): Although the profit is now realized through external sales, the consolidation worksheet still requires a beginning retained earnings adjustment because last year''s elimination was not recorded on the books.
