  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under GASB Statement No. 34, fiduciary activities are excluded from government-wide financial statements because the resources are held in trust or as an agent for external parties and are not available to finance the government''s own programs. They are reported separately in fiduciary fund financial statements.
Wrong (A): Legal administration does not make fiduciary resources governmental; the beneficiaries (retirees, school districts) are external parties.
Wrong (C): Neither fund qualifies as a component unit; both are fiduciary funds excluded entirely from government-wide statements regardless of type.
