-- Q700: Advanced Consolidations [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under ASC 805-10-25-10, in a step acquisition the previously held equity interest must be remeasured to fair value on the acquisition date. The gain equals fair value ($1,800,000) minus carrying value ($1,500,000) = $300,000, recognized in earnings. This ensures total consideration for goodwill reflects current fair values.
Wrong (A): ASC 805 explicitly requires remeasurement of previously held interests to fair value; ignoring this step would misstate goodwill.
Wrong (C): The $1,800,000 gain amount is incorrect (it equals the full fair value, not the gain), and the gain is recognized in earnings, not OCI.
Wrong (D): The $500,000 amount has no basis in the given facts, and the gain is recognized in earnings, not as an adjustment to goodwill.$EXPL$
